W_{ij} = \begin{cases} \sum_{p=1}^i \frac{1}{p} - \sum_{p=1}^{n-i} \frac{1}{p}, & i = j, \\ \frac{(-1)^{j-i} \binom{n}{i}}{j-i} \binom{n}{j}^{-1}, & i \neq j, \quad i,j = 0,1,\ldots,n. \end{cases}
REMARK 1. For the case i = j, setting p = i - k, we have \sum_{k=0, k \neq i}^n \frac{1}{i - k} = \sum_{k=0}^{i-1} \frac{1}{i - k} + \sum_{k=i+1}^n \frac{1}{i - k} = \sum_{p=1}^i \frac{1}{p} - \sum_{p=1}^{n-i} \frac{1}{p}

